[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: learning.EXAMPLES
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[EXAMPLES]
overview: Concrete examples of documentation updates
purpose: Show how to apply the self-learning process end-to-end

[EXAMPLE_1_USER_EXPLICIT_RULE]
scenario: User says "Never use ORM raw queries in service layer — they bypass our audit log"

step_1_identify:
  - From user (meets CRITERIA_1)
  - It's a constraint
  - Target: CONSTRAINTS.toon

step_2_locate:
  - Open docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon
  - Add as new [CONSTRAINT_N]

step_3_check_duplicate:
  - Search CONSTRAINTS.toon for "raw query" / "ORM"
  - Not found, proceed

step_4_write:
  [CONSTRAINT_N]
  rule: Never use raw ORM queries in the service layer
  why: Raw queries bypass the audit log, breaking compliance
  alternatives: Use the repository abstraction; if raw SQL is required, it must live in repository/
  enforcement: Code review veto if found outside repository/
  source: User explicit statement

step_5_edit: Use Edit tool to add to CONSTRAINTS.toon

step_6_verify:
  - File structure intact
  - TOON syntax valid
  - Constraint is clear

step_7_commit:
  git commit -m "docs: [constraint] prohibit raw ORM queries in service layer

  Source: User explicit statement
  File: docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[EXAMPLE_2_FOUND_IN_CODE]
scenario: Reading src/auth/session.py, found comment: "# MUST rotate keys every 30 days"

step_1_identify:
  - Found in code with MUST comment (meets CRITERIA_2)
  - It's an operational constraint
  - Target: CONSTRAINTS.toon (or domain-specific file like AUTH.toon if project has one)

step_2_locate:
  - Open docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon
  - Add as new [CONSTRAINT_N]

step_3_check_duplicate:
  - Search for "rotation" / "30 days"
  - Not found, proceed

step_4_write:
  [CONSTRAINT_N]
  rule: Session keys must rotate every 30 days
  why: Limits blast radius of key compromise (compliance)
  implementation: Timer in src/auth/session.py (look for ROTATION_INTERVAL)
  source: Code inspection, src/auth/session.py comment

step_5_edit: Update CONSTRAINTS.toon

step_6_verify:
  - Integrates with existing constraints
  - References actual code location
  - Clear and concise

step_7_commit:
  git commit -m "docs: [constraint] document session key rotation interval

  Source: Code inspection of src/auth/session.py
  File: docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[EXAMPLE_3_DISCOVERED_ARCHITECTURE]
scenario: While debugging, discovered that the API gateway pools HTTP connections per upstream and reuses them

step_1_identify:
  - Discovered from code analysis (meets CRITERIA_3)
  - Architectural pattern
  - Target: ARCHITECTURE.toon

step_2_locate:
  - Open docs/agent/ARCHITECTURE.toon
  - Find [API_GATEWAY] or create subsection under [COMPONENTS]

step_3_check_duplicate:
  - Search "connection pool" / "reuse"
  - Not found, proceed

step_4_write:
  [API_GATEWAY.CONNECTION_POOLING]
  mechanism: HTTP connections pooled per upstream host, reused across requests
  benefit: Reduces handshake overhead, improves P99 latency
  implementation: See gateway/client.go (pool size configurable per upstream)
  source: Code discovery while debugging timeout issue

step_5_edit: Update ARCHITECTURE.toon

step_6_verify:
  - Doesn't duplicate existing sections
  - Adds gateway-specific detail
  - References implementation file

step_7_commit:
  git commit -m "docs: [arch] document gateway connection pooling

  Source: Code discovery while analyzing gateway/client.go
  File: docs/agent/ARCHITECTURE.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[EXAMPLE_4_FIXING_ERROR]
scenario: PROJECT.toon says feature X is "IN_PROGRESS" but it's fully shipped and in production

step_1_identify:
  - Found error in docs (meets CRITERIA_4)
  - Target: PROJECT.toon

step_2_locate:
  - Open docs/agent/PROJECT.toon
  - Find [STATUS] section, feature X entry

step_3_check_duplicate:
  - This is the only entry for feature X, proceed

step_4_write:
  Change:
    status: IN_PROGRESS
  To:
    status: DONE
    completed: 2026-03-15
    notes: Deployed to production, all acceptance criteria met

step_5_edit: Update PROJECT.toon

step_6_verify:
  - Status matches reality
  - Dependent work items can now be unblocked

step_7_commit:
  git commit -m "docs: [project] mark feature X as completed

  Source: Verification that feature is live in production
  File: docs/agent/PROJECT.toon

  Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"

[WHAT_TO_AVOID]
example_bad_1:
  content: "The system is complex"
  problem: No actionable information

example_bad_2:
  content: "Probably the developers meant to implement it this way"
  problem: Vague, unverified speculation

example_bad_3:
  content: "This would be better if implemented differently"
  problem: Not a rule, just personal preference

example_bad_4:
  content: "The code iterates through elements"
  problem: Anyone reading code sees this

example_bad_5:
  content: "Vector grows by 2x when capacity exceeded"
  problem: Implementation detail, can change, not architectural

[KEY_TAKEAWAYS]
DO:
  - Small targeted updates (5-10 lines)
  - One file per update
  - Always verify source
  - Link to references (line numbers, existing docs)
  - Clear commit message with source attribution
  - Check for duplicates before adding

DON'T:
  - Large multi-concept updates
  - Speculative or opinion-based info
  - Obvious facts from code
  - Updates without source attribution
  - Break existing structure/format
  - Forget [docs] prefix in commit
